{
  "title": "Rendered decision header always reads \"[Decision 0\" — the counter \
never increments",
  "description": "Every decision rendered to the pilot carries the header \
\"[Decision 0, snapshot=N]\". Measured over 400 recorded rollout trajectories \
(20 GRPO steps x 20 games, Boros mirror): 29,906 rendered decisions, and the \
decision number is 0 in all 29,906. It never once increments. The snapshot \
field does vary, so the header is not frozen wholesale — only the decision \
counter is.\n\n\
Consequence: the model cannot tell turn 1 from turn 40. Trajectories here run \
to a median of 76 decisions and a max of 110, against a context window that \
keeps 40 at full fidelity and summarises 20 more, so a policy is routinely \
being asked to act deep in a game with no signal about how deep it is and with \
its own early history already evicted.\n\n\
This matters beyond cosmetics for work in progress on deck-general play: that \
design puts card text in the prompt once and measures whether the policy still \
uses text revealed many decisions earlier. Measuring distance-sensitivity with \
a render that never tells the policy its position confounds \"does not use \
far-back text\" with \"cannot tell what far-back means\".\n\n\
Repro: take any recorded game's rendered conversation and count distinct values \
of the capture in /\\[Decision (\\d+),/ across the whole trajectory. Expected: \
0..n-1. Actual: {0}.\n\n\
Found while measuring land-offer compliance against decision index; the index \
had to be recovered from the ordinal position of each header instead.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
